
                             ; SWEEPER: stands still and sweeps its radar
                             ; in 5-degree steps. On contact (RADAR reads
                             ; negative when a robot is in the beam), aims
                             ; along the radar bearing and fires a shell
                             ; timed to burst at the reported distance.
                             ; S grows without bound; RADAR and AIM both
                             ; wrap it mod 360 internally. The step is
                             ; jittered so two stationary robots can't
                             ; leave each other between rays forever.

      0 TO S                 ; S = radar bearing
      4 TO RANDOM            ; RANDOM now reads as 0..3

  LOOP
      S + 4 + RANDOM TO S    ; advance the sweep 4..7 degrees
      S TO RADAR             ; point the radar
      RADAR TO R             ; scan: negative means a robot at range -R
      IF R < 0 GOTO FIRE
      GOTO LOOP

  FIRE
      S TO AIM               ; shoot along the radar bearing
      0 - R TO SHOT          ; burst right on the contact
      GOTO LOOP
